Z||000000||Fiero5||11-27-2000||09:58 PM||||I am sitting here watching Carolina pounce all over Green Bay so far during the first half, and I am having to listen to Dennis Miller as he throws out his string of silly comments. <BR>I was wondering what the rest of you football lovers think of having Dennis Miller as co-color commentator on Monday Night Football?||||reg||5
Z||000001||hugh||11-27-2000||10:17 PM||||Give me Dan Dierdorf anytime.I'm not that big a fan,but Miller just doesn't cut it,It seems as if he is trying to impress us with his supposed knowledge and vocabulary.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||11-27-2000||10:39 PM||||Well, Bret Favre just tied it up with a 45 yard strike into the end zone. Wow, what an arm. This is quite a shoot out. Though some of the scores have come from silly turn overs.<P>I kinda liked Boomer when he was in the booth with the guys last year. Of course, I am kinda biased due to the fact that Boomer is one of my favorite Bengal players :o)<BR>Can we as football fans vote Dennis Miller outa there??||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||11-27-2000||10:55 PM||||BOOMER! BOOMER! BOOMER!<BR>Yeah, he did good.<BR>I'm glad I work nights cause I never liked D.M.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||11-27-2000||11:01 PM||||I'm not sure exactly what I said when I found out he would be on Monday Night Football, but it was something like,<P>Ohh joy...<P>Gosh, if they're going to put a comedian in there, why didn't they choose someone like Jim Carrey or something?  I know he'd push the commentator salary cap, but think about how interesting it would be!<P><BR>Other canidates of the top of my head:<P>Tom Green<BR>Beavis & Butthead<BR>Regis<BR>Peter Jennings<BR>I'd better stop now...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||11-28-2000||02:47 AM||||Regis Philbn with the Play by Play, Bill Clinton with color commentary!<P>"Jones has the ball on the 50, the 40 the 30, I'M GOING OUTTA MY MIND HERE!!!"<P>"Ya know, his mom is kinda hot. Anybody got some Miracle Whip for this sandwich?  And an RC? Thanks, honey."<P>"Hey Mr. President, ya mind? WE GOT A GAME HERE!!! I"M GOING OUTTA MY MIND!"<P>"Hey Regis, I just want to say, I did not pat that waitress on the ass. Unless of course you have a different definition of patting her ass."<P>"Mr. President, YOU'RE DRIVING ME MAD, I TELL YA!" ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||11-28-2000||08:42 AM||||I love Dennis Millers HBO show, he is my favorite comedian.  Also, he is VERY smart in case any of you didn't know that.<P>However, on MNF he just doesn't click.  Some of his comments, while they may be funny, just seem a little off the wall for a football game.  Everything normal he says sounds scripted.  I give him credit for trying but I think after this season he should hang it up<P>  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||11-28-2000||09:14 AM||||Can't say I'm a Dennis Miller fan.  Al Michaels and Dan Fouts would be great by themselves - Fouts knows the game inside and out, and Michaels just might be the best play-by-play guy of all time.  Miller adds nothing.  He's not admirably intelligent, he's condescendingly intelligent.||||reg||13
Z||000008||turbo86se||11-28-2000||02:49 PM||||Personally, I really didn't think he'd last this long. I'm not really a DM fan, but I'll watch MNF anyways. I didn't think Carolina would pull it off, then again I'm a Colts fan. <P>If Regis were to be the next commentary, I'd never watch MNF again, man he's annoying!! ||||reg||1
Z||000009||RiceCooker||11-28-2000||02:59 PM||||I hate their political approach to bad ratings. If their ratings have gone down in the last few years, maybe people watch all of their footbal on Sundays, maybe there are better shows on TV on mondays, maybe Monday is bowling night. <BR>So they try to go out and make ratings better by trying to attract non football viewers? It just does not make any sense. If you don't really like football all that much and you want to watch something funny on TV. you won't turn to MNF to laugh at Dennis Miller, you will still go to the comedy network.<BR>Furthermore (that's a great word for essays) Dennis Miller is way to conscious about his purpose there. He tries wayyyyyyyy to hard to say something funny. <BR>Who else thinks he has one of the Whiniest voices in the history of mankind?<BR>AAAAARRRRRGGGGGGHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!!<BR>It gets me all wotked up just talkin about it!<BR>It makes football guys like myself NOT want to watch MNF.<BR>(I'm yelling now if you couldn't tell)||||reg||1
